# Wendy Beauty & Spa — Full Stack (Next.js + Supabase)

The real backend: a Postgres database (via Supabase) behind an admin
dashboard, with the same premium storefront on top. Products, homepage
content, bookings, enquiries, team and reviews are all editable from
`/admin` — no code changes needed for day-to-day updates.

## Stack

- **Next.js 14** (App Router, TypeScript, Server Actions)
- **Supabase**: Postgres database, Auth (admin login), Storage (product/banner photos)
- **Deployed on Vercel**, same as the front-end-only version

Cart and wishlist still live in the visitor's browser (localStorage) — there's
still no payment gateway, by design: every "Add to Bag" or booking is an
**enquiry**, confirmed by your team on WhatsApp, matching the original brief.

