## 1. Create your Supabase project

1. Go to [supabase.com](https://supabase.com) → **New project**. Pick a name, a
   database password (save it somewhere), and a region close to Nigeria (EU
   West / Frankfurt is usually fastest).
2. Once it's ready, open **SQL Editor**, paste the contents of
   `supabase/schema.sql`, and click **Run**. This creates every table, the
   security rules (RLS) that keep customer data private, and a public storage
   bucket for photos.
3. *(Optional)* Paste and run `supabase/seed.sql` too, for some starting
   sample products so the site isn't empty on first load.
4. Create your admin login: **Authentication → Users → Add user** — set an
   email and password (this is what you'll use to sign in at `/admin`).
5. Copy that user's **UID** (shown in the users table), go back to
   **SQL Editor**, and run:
   ```sql
   insert into admin_users (user_id) values ('paste-the-uid-here');
   ```
   This is what actually grants admin access — creating a login alone isn't
   enough, on purpose, so a stray signup can never reach the dashboard.
6. Go to **Settings → API** and copy the **Project URL** and **anon public
   key** — you'll need these next.

## 2. Configure the app

```bash
cd wendy-beauty-spa-app
cp .env.example .env.local
```
Paste your Project URL and anon key into `.env.local`.

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```
Visit `http://localhost:3000` for the storefront and
`http://localhost:3000/admin` to sign in with the login you created above.

## 3. Push to GitHub

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Wendy Beauty & Spa — full stack"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/wendy-beauty-spa.git
git push -u origin main
```

## 4. Deploy on Vercel

1. [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) → **Add New… → Project** → import the
   GitHub repo. Framework preset: **Next.js** (auto-detected).
2. Before deploying, add the environment variables from `.env.local` under
   **Settings → Environment Variables**:
   - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
   - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
3. Click **Deploy**. Every future `git push` to `main` redeploys
   automatically, database and all — nothing else to configure.

