## What's editable from `/admin`, without touching code

| Section | What it controls |
|---|---|
| Products | Name, category, description, price (or "on request"), availability, badge, colors, sizes, photo |
| Homepage | Hero headline/subtext/CTA and any other homepage banner |
| Bookings | Every Beauty & Spa appointment request, with a status you update as you follow up |
| Enquiries | A log of "Request Order Confirmation" taps from customer bags |
| Team | Team member names, role groups, photos |
| Reviews | Genuine customer reviews (unpublished by default — nothing shows until you approve it) |
| Settings | Both WhatsApp numbers, contact email, site tagline |

## Security notes

- `/admin` is gated two ways: `middleware.ts` redirects signed-out visitors
  to the login page, **and** every database write is independently checked
  against the `admin_users` table by Postgres itself (Row Level Security).
  Even if someone bypassed the app entirely, the database would still refuse
  their writes.
- Never commit `.env.local` — it's already in `.gitignore`.
- The anon key is meant to be public (it's used in the browser); what keeps
  data safe is the RLS policies in `schema.sql`, not keeping that key secret.

## Extending it further

- **Payments**: add Paystack or Flutterwave once you're ready to charge
  directly instead of confirming orders on WhatsApp.
- **Email notifications**: a Supabase Edge Function + Resend/SendGrid can
  email you the moment a booking or enquiry comes in, instead of checking
  `/admin` manually.
- **SEO/sitemap**: `app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts` can be added the same
  way as any Next.js route if you want them generated dynamically from your
  product list.
